=== LINES ===
[000] indent=0 block=335dbe27 H1
      "# " {b fg=#337ea9}
      "😎 "
      "Core Applications 2026 Vision" {b fg=#337ea9}
[001] indent=0 block=-
[002] indent=2 block=335dbe27 H2
      "## " {b fg=#337ea9}
      "Why We're Building This" {b fg=#337ea9}
[003] indent=0 block=-
[004] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "Through our design sprints, customer research, and direct work with "
[005] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "enterprise customers, we heard the same pain point over and over: "
[006] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "workflow fragmentation. Traders spend hours every morning toggling "
[007] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "between weather sites, market data platforms, spreadsheets, and "
[008] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "internal tools just to build a picture of what kind of day it is. "
[009] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "The analysis that should take 10 minutes takes two hours, and most "
[010] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "of that time is gathering context, not making decisions. "
[011] indent=0 block=-
[012] indent=4 block=33bdbe27
      "Two things are driving this effort: we have emerging product-market "
[013] indent=4 block=33bdbe27
      "fit with our enterprise customers, and the competitive landscape has"
[014] indent=4 block=33bdbe27
      "shifted with agentic AI. We're doubling down on what's working, with"
[015] indent=4 block=33bdbe27
      "some targeted tweaks."
[016] indent=0 block=-
[017] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "Our enterprise engagements (NRG, BP, Gunvor) have validated that "
[018] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "EQ's platform solves real problems for real traders. But enterprise "
[019] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "sales cycles are long, resource-intensive, and vulnerable to single "
[020] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "points of failure if there are skeptical users. We are targeting the"
[021] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "hardest, most expensive place to enter a customer relationship: the "
[022] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "top of the enterprise. A common application suite with progressive "
[023] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "access levels changes this for our customers and for us.  An "
[024] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "individual trader signs up and immediately gets value of workflow "
[025] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "fragmentation relief through unified market data, probabilistic "
[026] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "forecasts, AI-native capabilities, and full transparency into the "
[027] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "data behind every assumption (what we call \"glass box\"). No "
[028] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "enterprise sales cycle required. We build brand rapport with "
[029] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "individual users, then provide the right hooks and carrots to "
[030] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "encourage them deeper into our enterprise solutions. This is the "
[031] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "tweaked GTM motion: lower friction entry, brand recognition with "
[032] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "individual users, and natural expansion into team and enterprise "
[033] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "contracts."
[034] indent=0 block=-
[035] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "As customers invest more, the platform grows with them. Bring your "
[036] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "own data, forecasts, and strategies into the same unified surface, "
[037] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "and our AI workflows seamlessly pick them up. Connect your existing "
[038] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "pipelines through our APIs and SDKs. Our enterprise platform "
[039] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "offering is the infrastructure that enables traders to understand "
[040] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "markets, evaluate positions, and take action, whether EQ develops "
[041] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "strategies for them or they develop their own."
[042] indent=0 block=-
[043] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "What makes this approach sticky is not any single feature. It's that"
[044] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "each layer of investment compounds. Workflow embedding gets us in "
[045] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "(traders adopt because it replaces the 20-tab morning routine, not "
[046] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "because we sold them a feature list). Speaking trader language from "
[047] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "day one means zero learning curve due to exceptional UX. "
[048] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "Co-optimization across market products (DART + CRRs + futures + gas "
[049] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "on one platform) creates value no individual tool can replicate. And"
[050] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "intelligence that learns, remembers, and compounds over time means a"
[051] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "trader who's used the product for six months has a system that "
[052] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "understands how they think. Switching means starting over."
[053] indent=0 block=-
[054] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[055] indent=0 block=-
[056] indent=4 block=335dbe27
[057] indent=0 block=-
[058] indent=2 block=335dbe27 H2
      "## " {b fg=#337ea9}
      "The Beta Build (Launch Target TBD pending scoping)" {b fg=#337ea9}
[059] indent=0 block=-
[060] indent=4 block=335dbe27 H3
      "### " {b}
      "Individual Trader Beta - Q2 Target (Marketed as “The Helm”)" {b}
[061] indent=0 block=-
[062] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "What it is:" {b}
      " Invite-only beta, ~12-20 users, full-featured trial. "
[063] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Design partner program that validates the PLG motion and generates"
[064] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "real usage data."
[065] indent=0 block=-
[066] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Features Scope:" {b}
[067] indent=0 block=-
[068] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "Explorer:" {b}
      " Probabilistic price forecasts, market data, constraint"
[069] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "analysis, system-wide views. Unified data layer replacing the "
[070] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "20-tab workflow."
[071] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "AI Chat:" {b}
      " Agentic analysis grounded in EQ's 60+ code frameworks. "
[072] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "Not generic summaries; power-industry-native intelligence with "
[073] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "full transparency on reasoning."
[074] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "Constraints deep dive:" {b}
      " Automated backstory and context for "
[075] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "individual constraints (the \"hour of research in 10 minutes\" use"
[076] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "case)."
[077] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "Lineage (fast follow):" {b}
      " DAG visibility showing data sources, "
[078] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "transformations, and point-in-time correctness. Every number has"
[079] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "a receipt."
[080] indent=0 block=-
[081] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "JTBD Scope:" {b}
[082] indent=0 block=-
[083] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to understand what kind of day tomorrow is as "
[084] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "quickly as possible"
[085] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to be able to do constraint analysis before "
[086] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "bid close to find potential high-return opportunities"
[087] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to ask a question and get an answer grounded "
[088] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "in power market fundamentals, not generic AI"
[089] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I don’t trust others to understand the complexities "
[090] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "of my work, so I want to be able to interrogate all of the "
[091] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "assumptions that i’m provided (forecasts, chat responses, market"
[092] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "summaries, etc)"
[093] indent=0 block=-
[094] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "What is NOT in beta:" {b}
[095] indent=0 block=-
[096] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "No portfolio data"
[097] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "No SCED what-if scenarios"
[098] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "No strategy/forecast workbench"
[099] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "No BYO Forecast integration"
[100] indent=0 block=-
[101] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Science dependencies for beta:" {b}
      " Minimal. Beta uses existing "
[102] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "probabilistic forecasts and market data already in the platform. "
[103] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "No new model development required."
[104] indent=0 block=-
[105] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Architecture:" {b}
      " Beta proceeds without ArchV2. Learnings from beta "
[106] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "feed ArchV2 requirements. Beta stack to be defined by engineering "
[107] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "& infrastructure."
[108] indent=0 block=-
[109] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Release cadence:" {b}
      " New feature every 1-2 weeks. Feedback loop "
[110] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "through release notes + direct user feedback requests."
[111] indent=0 block=-
[112] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Beta users:" {b}
      " Currently users from 2+ companies. Max 20 users total."
[113] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Controlled rollout, not public."
[114] indent=0 block=-
[115] indent=4 block=335dbe27 H3
      "### " {b}
      "6-Month Vision (End of Q3 MVP)" {b}
[116] indent=0 block=-
[117] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Q3 MVP (OKR2.2 Target: October)"
[118] indent=0 block=-
[119] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "What it is:" {b}
      " A self-serve, low friction entry point onto our "
[120] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "platform and application suite not limited to design partners"
[121] indent=0 block=-
[122] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "What changes from beta to MVP:" {b}
[123] indent=0 block=-
[124] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "Users can self-serve sign-up and pay with credit card"
[125] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "Core Applications & SA & Delivery propose feature graduation "
[126] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "criteria by end of beta based on customer usage and feedback"
[127] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "GTM finalize pricing plan"
[128] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "• "
      "OKR1.5: […] The Helm "
      "MVP" {i}
      " by end of Q3’26. Add 20 paid "
[129] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "  "
      "subscribers by the end of Q4’26 to drive $60K in new ARR."
[130] indent=0 block=-
[131] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Architecture" {b}
      ": Multi-tenant environment, detailed requirements to "
[132] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "be put together with engineering & infrastructure"
[133] indent=0 block=-
[134] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Release cadence: " {b}
      "Continue our Beta momentum with new features "
[135] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "every 1-2 weeks. Ideally SA & Delivery also can choose to release "
[136] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "these features to enterprise customers."
[137] indent=0 block=-
[138] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[139] indent=0 block=-
[140] indent=2 block=335dbe27 H2
      "## " {b fg=#337ea9}
      "Application Suite 2-Year Vision (2026 – 2028)" {b fg=#337ea9}
[141] indent=0 block=-
[142] indent=4 block=335dbe27 H3
      "### " {b}
      "One Product That Grows With You" {b}
[143] indent=0 block=-
[144] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "This is one application suite. It starts as an individual trader's"
[145] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "daily operating environment and scales as customers invest more: "
[146] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "more data, more users, more automation, more integration. We use "
[147] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "\"doors\" to describe natural expansion moments, not tiers or gates,"
[148] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "because a customer can enter through any door and does not need to"
[149] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "proceed sequentially. Each door is an \"I want more\" signal where "
[150] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "the platform meets the customer where they are. There are value "
[151] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "levers that can be controlled throughout the application to help "
[152] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "control the funnel and GTM motion as well (usage caps, limitations"
[153] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "on scenarios, limitations on agents, etc.)."
[154] indent=0 block=-
[155] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Door 1: Individual Trader" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want an army of analysts at my " {i}
[156] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "back\"" {i}
[157] indent=0 block=-
[158] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "An individual trader signs up and gets immediate value: unified "
[159] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "market data, probabilistic forecasts at every node, constraint "
[160] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "analysis with automated AI investigation, cross-commodity views, "
[161] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "and full system visualization with weather, wind, and temperature "
[162] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "layers over time. Glass box transparency on every number. But this"
[163] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "isn't just a dashboard. From day one, traders have agents that "
[164] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "help them explore: research a constraint move, investigate a price"
[165] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "spike, run a scenario to test an intuition, generate a performance"
[166] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "attribution report. AI chat grounded in EQ's analytical frameworks"
[167] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "turns questions into analysis, not just answers. The platform "
[168] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "learns the trader's patterns, preferences, and past analyses "
[169] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "through personal context memory. Custom views, saved prompts, and "
[170] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "personalized layouts make it theirs."
[171] indent=0 block=-
[172] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "JTBD → grow from “Help me understand” (Beta) to “help me "
[173] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "investigate and act on my thinking”"
[174] indent=0 block=-
[175] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to test a hypothesis about what happens to my "
[176] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "positions if gas spikes or wind drops, without building a "
[177] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "spreadsheet"
[178] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to be alerted when something changes that "
[179] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "affects my positions, not discover it during my morning routine"
[180] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want the system to remember my patterns and "
[181] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "preferences so it gets smarter the more I use it"
[182] indent=0 block=-
[183] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Door 2: My Data" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want my data and forecasts in here\"" {i}
[184] indent=0 block=-
[185] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Customers bring their own forecasts, proprietary data, and market "
[186] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "views into the same unified surface. This triggers an isolated "
[187] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "environment and unlocks a vertical AI for power which includes "
[188] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "portfolio-aware AI and memory. The platform now reasons over their"
[189] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "world, not just the market. Our AI workflows seamlessly pick up "
[190] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "customer data alongside EQ's, organized, versioned, and queryable."
[191] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "EQ offers white-glove service to make this an exceptional "
[192] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "experience for our customers with integrations starting at this "
[193] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "point and at every integration point in the additional doors. "
[194] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "These engagements are where Product learns what to 'productize'. "
[195] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "The patterns SA & Delivery sees across enterprise customers become"
[196] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "the templates and workflows that scale through the offering."
[197] indent=0 block=-
[198] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "JTBD → shifts from EQ’s world to the customer’s own alpha"
[199] indent=0 block=-
[200] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want the same AI and analysis capabilities applied "
[201] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "to my proprietary data, not just market data"
[202] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a user, I want to bring my own forecasts in and see them with"
[203] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "the same glass box treatment"
[204] indent=0 block=-
[205] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Door 3: My Strategies" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want to build and run strategies on " {i}
[206] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "this\"" {i}
[207] indent=0 block=-
[208] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "The shift from exploration to operations. Door 1 agents help you "
[209] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "understand the market. Door 3 expands to run your trading "
[210] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "business. Strategy pipelines, automated briefings, backtesting "
[211] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "across historical conditions. Agents that follow Science and "
[212] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Strategy's proven analytical workflows: run a DART analysis, "
[213] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "evaluate a CRR position, stress-test a gas portfolio using the "
[214] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "same artifacts and methodologies our quants use internally. The "
[215] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "platform tracks what worked and why through operational memory. "
[216] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Co-optimization across market products (DART + CRRs + futures + "
[217] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "gas) creates value no individual tool can replicate. The 2-year "
[218] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "trajectory is from EQ-assisted to fully self-serve. Customers have"
[219] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "told us directly that they want to build it themselves. Product's "
[220] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "job is to make that possible by turning what we've learned from "
[221] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "enterprise engagements into capabilities any user can access "
[222] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "independently."
[223] indent=0 block=-
[224] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "JTBD → shifts from analysis to operations"
[225] indent=0 block=-
[226] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a trader, I want to be able to easily research, build, "
[227] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "monitor, and deploy strategies"
[228] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a trader, I want to evaluate how my strategy performs across "
[229] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "a range of market conditions before I commit capital"
[230] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a trader, I want to know what's actually driving my PnL"
[231] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a desk, we want to see our portfolio together, understand our"
[232] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "strategy interactions and behaviors, and maximize risk adjusted "
[233] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "return across all of our individual work"
[234] indent=0 block=-
[235] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "Door 4: My Team" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want my team to have these capabilities\"" {i}
[236] indent=0 block=-
[237] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "A desk lead notices the value. Shared workspaces, team memory that"
[238] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "cross-pollinates context across the desk, shared prompt libraries "
[239] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "and agent results. The buying authority shifts from personal "
[240] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "credit card to team budget. The transition is concierge-assisted, "
[241] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "not a migration."
[242] indent=0 block=-
[243] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "JTBD → grows from individual to collective intelligence"
[244] indent=0 block=-
[245] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "• "
      "As a desk lead, I want my team to share context without "
[246] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "  "
      "scheduling a meeting"
[247] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "• "
      "As a team, we want our best analyst's research to benefit "
[248] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "  "
      "everyone, not live in one person's head or desktop"
[249] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "• "
      "As a desk lead, I want visibility into what my team is watching "
[250] indent=6 block=33bdbe27
      "  "
      "and what they might be missing"
[251] indent=0 block=-
[252] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Door 5: My Enterprise" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want to embed PowerOS into my systems\"" {i}
[253] indent=0 block=-
[254] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "The product is no longer standalone. SDK access, API integrations,"
[255] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "ETRM/EMS connectors. Customer engineering teams build on EQ's "
[256] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "primitives. DAG-driven real-time updates as new data arrives. "
[257] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Cross-system reasoning and memory span EQ and connected tools. "
[258] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "SSO, compliance certifications, self-serve extensions."
[259] indent=0 block=-
[260] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a technical user, I want to build on EQ's capabilities with "
[261] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "my own tools and code, not be limited to what the UI offers"
[262] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a firm, I want my team to be able to build, modify, and "
[263] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "maintain our own workflows on this platform without submitting a"
[264] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "ticket and waiting for EQ to do it for us"
[265] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As an engineering team, I want one API surface that works the "
[266] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "same way whether I'm powering a dashboard, an automated "
[267] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "pipeline, or an agent"
[268] indent=0 block=-
[269] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Door 6: Self-Service" {b}
      " — "
      "\"I want this running my org\"" {i}
[270] indent=0 block=-
[271] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "Org-wide deployment, cross-desk intelligence, institutional memory"
[272] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "that compounds over years. Users build their own workflows, "
[273] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "agents, and strategies on the platform. Full self-serve "
[274] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "application customization: users vibe-code their own views and "
[275] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "tools. A trader who's been on the Helm for six months has a system"
[276] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "that understands how they think. An organization that's been on it"
[277] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "for a year has an institutional memory that no individual "
[278] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "departure can erase. This is where EQ's moat becomes existential, "
[279] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "because switching means starting over."
[280] indent=0 block=-
[281] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a head of trading, I want intelligence that compounds across "
[282] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "desks, not just within them. What the gas desk learns about a "
[283] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "regime shift should inform the power desk automatically."
[284] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a COO, I want institutional knowledge that survives when my "
[285] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "best trader leaves"
[286] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "• "
      "As a firm, I want my people building their own tools and "
[287] indent=6 block=336dbe27
      "  "
      "workflows on this platform, not waiting for a vendor roadmap"
[288] indent=0 block=-
[289] indent=4 block=335dbe27 H3
      "### " {b}
      "What This Requires From the Platform" {b}
[290] indent=0 block=-
[291] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "The doors describe what customers experience. Underneath, the "
[292] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "platform needs to evolve to support it. That's where architecture "
[293] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "v2 comes in."
[294] indent=0 block=-
[295] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "We want to make sure SA & Delivery can easily deploy core features"
[296] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "from the core application suite to enterprise customers, that we "
[297] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "can grow our capabilities horizontally FAST, and that we can "
[298] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "explore > build > ship new features in fast iteration. We also "
[299] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "want to make sure there's alignment between the APIs & primitives "
[300] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "that power internal applications, customer-facing integrations, "
[301] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "and agents so we can provide a unified customer experience. Agents"
[302] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "are present from Door 1 (scenario agents, research agents) and "
[303] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "scale in sophistication through Door 6 (org-wide agent fleets, "
[304] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "custom-trained models). The infrastructure needs to support the "
[305] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "full spectrum."
[306] indent=0 block=-
[307] indent=6 block=335dbe27
      "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[308] indent=0 block=-
[309] indent=2 block=335dbe27 H2
      "## " {b fg=#337ea9}
      "How This Connects to Science & Algorithms + Trading Teams" {b fg=#337ea9}
[310] indent=0 block=-
[311] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "Beta (now – June):" {b}
      " Science dependencies are minimal. Existing "
[312] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "probabilistic forecasts and market data. No new model development "
[313] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "needed for beta scope."
[314] indent=0 block=-
[315] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "MVP (Q3):" {b}
      " MVP Science scope to be defined jointly with Tyler based "
[316] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "on beta signal. What-if is not critical path for MVP."
[317] indent=0 block=-
[318] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "2-Year:" {b}
      " Central to the full vision. SCED what-if scenarios, "
[319] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "co-optimization across market products, new market expansion (gas, "
[320] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "futures, ftrs, etc.). EQ's application suite makes our best thinking"
[321] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "accessible at scale. Workflows, skills, and predefined artifacts "
[322] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "turn proven methodologies into capabilities any user can leverage, "
[323] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "whether EQ develops the strategies or the customer develops their "
[324] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "own."
[325] indent=0 block=-
[326] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[327] indent=0 block=-
[328] indent=2 block=335dbe27 H2
      "## " {b fg=#337ea9}
      "Open Questions" {b fg=#337ea9}
[329] indent=0 block=-
[330] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "1. "
      "How do we communicate the application suite framing externally? "
[331] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "   "
      "(naming is \"early discovery,\" not finalized for GTM)"
[332] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "2. "
      "ArchV2 sequencing: how does Helm beta feed ArchV2 priorities vs. "
[333] indent=4 block=335dbe27
      "   "
      "other demand signals?"
